cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "relu-tanh-asinh: a conjugate f/g residual layer"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: PureTearsDropped
repository-code: "https://github.com/PureTearsDropped/relu-tanh-asinh"
license: 0BSD
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22847920
abstract: >-
  A residual layer built from a conjugate pair: a saturating neuron f (ReLU
  above zero, tanh below) and a decoder g (ReLU above, asinh below) that is
  deliberately not f's inverse. The mismatch is what produces the
  nonlinearity; to leading order it is -a^2/(2b^2) x^3. Measured against
  plain MLPs and SwiGLU on a teacher-student task built so that depth
  genuinely matters; SwiGLU wins. Includes an honest record of two
  conclusions that were withdrawn after checking them, and the benchmark
  diagnostics that would have caught both.
keywords:
  - activation function
  - residual network
  - quantisation
  - ternary weights
  - benchmark methodology
  - negative results
